$DIR/test.p:88:70: variants A and B of packed union P both have tag value 1
    The values after case in a packed union variant are the tag values that
    select it. Each must be a constant of the tag's type that fits in the tag's
    bits, and no value may select two variants, so that every bit pattern means
    at most one variant.
    (see "Unions" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.13)
    (run "pluto explain E2408" for a longer explanation)
